    "title": "Proteinuria and Glucose Trace on Urinalysis",
    "message": "The patient's urinalysis shows protein 1+ and glucose trace. Proteinuria is a marker of kidney damage, consistent with the declining eGFR and potentially related to TDF toxicity or NSAID use. A trace of glucose in the absence of known diabetes warrants evaluation for new-onset diabetes, which is a comorbidity that can compound renal and cardiovascular risk. Guidelines note that uncontrolled diabetes can lead to complications like chronic kidney disease.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
